Sval: put Windows' backdrop only behind a see-through window

Sval turns on widget.windows.mica for a Workspace colour's transparency.
The pref also turns on the -moz-windows-mica media query in every window,
and Firefox's rules under it make a browser window's root transparent with
its own grey wash. A Sval window that is not see-through would then show
through with no backdrop behind it. Sval draws a see-through window's
colour itself (sval-panel.css) and sets windowsmica on the root only while
it is see-through (sval-panel-appearance.js), so the attribute leaves the
markup and Firefox's Mica rules go.

